---Represents a REST API.
---@class aws.api_gateway.RestApi
---@field id? aws.api_gateway.String The API's identifier. This identifier is unique across all of your APIs in API Gateway.
---@field name? aws.api_gateway.String The API's name.
---@field description? aws.api_gateway.String The API's description.
---@field createdDate? aws.api_gateway.Timestamp The timestamp when the API was created.
---@field version? aws.api_gateway.String A version identifier for the API.
---@field warnings? aws.api_gateway.ListOfString The warning messages reported when failonwarnings is turned on during API import.
---@field binaryMediaTypes? aws.api_gateway.ListOfString The list of binary media types supported by the RestApi. By default, the RestApi supports only UTF-8-encoded text payloads.
---@field minimumCompressionSize? aws.api_gateway.NullableInteger A nullable integer that is used to enable compression (with non-negative between 0 and 10485760 (10M) bytes, inclusive) or disable compression (with a null value) on an API. When compression is enabled, compression or decompression is not applied on the payload if the payload size is smaller than this value. Setting it to zero allows compression for any payload size.
---@field apiKeySource? aws.api_gateway.ApiKeySourceType The source of the API key for metering requests according to a usage plan. Valid values are: >HEADER to read the API key from the X-API-Key header of a request. AUTHORIZER to read the API key from the UsageIdentifierKey from a custom authorizer.
---@field endpointConfiguration? aws.api_gateway.EndpointConfiguration The endpoint configuration of this RestApi showing the endpoint types and IP address types of the API.
---@field policy? aws.api_gateway.String A stringified JSON policy document that applies to this RestApi regardless of the caller and Method configuration.
---@field tags? aws.api_gateway.MapOfStringToString The collection of tags. Each tag element is associated with a given resource.
---@field disableExecuteApiEndpoint aws.api_gateway.Boolean Specifies whether clients can invoke your API by using the default execute-api endpoint. By default, clients can invoke your API with the default https://{api_id}.execute-api.{region}.amazonaws.com endpoint. To require that clients use a custom domain name to invoke your API, disable the default endpoint.
---@field rootResourceId? aws.api_gateway.String The API's root resource ID.
---@field securityPolicy? aws.api_gateway.SecurityPolicy The Transport Layer Security (TLS) version + cipher suite for this RestApi.
---@field endpointAccessMode? aws.api_gateway.EndpointAccessMode The endpoint access mode of the RestApi.
---@field apiStatus? aws.api_gateway.ApiStatus The ApiStatus of the RestApi.
---@field apiStatusMessage? aws.api_gateway.String The status message of the RestApi. When the status message is UPDATING you can still invoke it.

